{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0601-prediction-and-evaluation-in-college-hockey.md", "equation": "Evaluation data:** actual NCAA tournament games (15 games per tournament, single elimination; 17 tournaments × 15 games = 255 games for the cumulative Bayes-factor study).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0601-prediction-and-evaluation-in-college-hockey.md", "equation": "Bayesian Bradley-Terry:** log-strengths λ_i ∈ (−∞,∞); win probability θ_ij = e^{λ_i}/(e^{λ_i}+e^{λ_j}) = logistic(λ_i − λ_j) (eq. 1.1). Likelihood: P(D|{λ_i}) = ∏_{i}∏_{j=i+1}^{t} θ_ij^{w_ij}(1−θ_ij)^{n_ij−w_ij} (eqs. 1.2–1.3); log-likelihood = Σ_i v_i λ_i − ½Σ_{i,j} n_ij ln(e^{λ_i}+e^{λ_j}) (eq. 1.4); MLE moment condition v_i = Σ_j n_ij θ̂_ij (eq. 1.5), solved by Ford's iteration (eq. 1.6). MLE is defined only up to an additive constant.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0601-prediction-and-evaluation-in-college-hockey.md", "equation": "D,I) = ∫ P(O | {λ̃_i}) (§2.1); (2) Gaussian approximation — Taylor-expand log-posterior at MAP; Hessian H_ij = −n_ij θ̃_ij θ̃_ji + δ_ij Σ_k θ̃_ik θ̃_ki − (prior term) (eq. 2.3); logistic-prior term δ_ij θ̃_{i0}(1−θ̃_{i0}) (eq. 2.4); Gaussian-prior term δ_ij/σ² (eq. 2.5); covariance Σ = H^{−1}, or the Moore-Penrose pseudo-inverse for the Haldane prior because of the one degenerate direction ℓ^{(1)} = (1/√t,…,1/√t), zero eigenvalue h₁=0 (eqs. 2.6–2.8); Monte Carlo estimate (eqs. 2.9–2.10) with N samples from N_t({λ̃_i},{Σ_ij}); (3) importance sampling — reweight by w_s ∝ f/g (eqs. 2.11–2.12), noted to be unstable when the posterior tail exceeds the Gaussian's (Figs. 1–3; the 59-dof χ distribution of normalized distance sits 5–10σ out, so heavy-tailed Student-t proposals make things worse, §2.3; skew-normal suggested as future work).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0601-prediction-and-evaluation-in-college-hockey.md", "equation": "Evaluation via Bayes factor (§3.1):** B_12 = P(O | M₀,D,I) = 2^{−n_O} (eq. 3.3); B_mle,0 = ∏_{g=1}^{n_O} 2θ̂_{w_g l_g} — each correctly-called game multiplies the factor by up to 2, each miss divides.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0602-measuring-spatial-allocative-efficiency-in-basketball.md", "equation": "Permutation test (§4.1):** test statistic T = Σ_iΣ_j v_i·ξ̃_ij·(A_ij − A†_ij) (eqs. 12–14) vs. 500 random permutations; one-sided p̂ = fraction < 0.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0603-understanding-and-pushing-the-limits-of.md", "equation": "English Premier League results + Bet365 odds from football-data.co.uk; M=20 teams, N=380 games per season (home+away round robin), ten seasons 2009–10 through 2018–19.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0603-understanding-and-pushing-the-limits-of.md", "equation": "Binary model:** Pr{i⋗j|θᵢ,θⱼ} = Φ(θᵢ−θⱼ), Φ logistic CDF Φ(v) = 1/(1+10^{−v/σ}) (eq. 5); FIFA uses σ=600, FIDE σ=400; ratings identified only up to additive origin and σ-scale.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0603-understanding-and-pushing-the-limits-of.md", "equation": "Elo = SG-ML:** negative log-likelihood J_n(θ) (eqs. 10–14, convex) minimized by stochastic gradient, one step per game: θ̂_{n+1,i} = θ̂_{n,i} + K[s_i − Φ(Δ_i)] (eqs. 22–25), s_i ∈ {1, 1/2, 0}, K absorbing 1/σ′. Absorbing μ → K gives the classical Elo update.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0603-understanding-and-pushing-the-limits-of.md", "equation": "Implicit draw model (Proposition 1):** the s_i = 1/2 convention is exactly SG-ML under Φ_H(v) = Φ²(v), Φ_A(v) = Φ²(−v), Φ_D(v) = 2Φ(v)Φ(−v) (eqs. 28–29; proof via squaring Φ(v)+Φ(−v)=1, eq. 30). Prediction semantics: Pr(win) = Φ²(Δ), Pr(draw) = 2Φ(Δ)Φ(−Δ) (eqs. 40–42). Crucially, the \"expected score\" E[s_i] = Φ(Δ_i) (eq. 45) is NOT the win probability — using Φ(Δ) as win probability under draws is the paper's central identified confusion.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0603-understanding-and-pushing-the-limits-of.md", "equation": "κ-Elo (Davidson 1970):** Φ_κ(v) = 10^{0.5v/σ}/(10^{0.5v/σ}+10^{−0.5v/σ}+κ) (eqs. 47–49), Φ_D(v) = κ√(Φ_H(v)Φ_A(v)); update θ̂_{n+1,i} = θ̂_{n,i} + K[s_i − F_κ(Δ_i)] (eq. 60) with F_κ(v) = (10^{v/2}+κ/2)/(10^{v/2}+10^{−v/2}+κ) (eq. 57). κ=0 recovers binary Elo; κ=2 ≈ classical Elo's implicit model up to scale (eq. 50).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0603-understanding-and-pushing-the-limits-of.md", "equation": "Frequency calibration:** p̄_D ≈ κ/(2+κ) (eq. 63); invert to κ̄ ≈ 2p̄_D/(1−p̄_D) (eq. 64). EPL p̄_D ≈ 0.25 → κ̄ ≈ 0.7. Classical κ=2 implicitly assumes p̄_D ≈ 0.5 — false in every competition where Elo is used.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0603-understanding-and-pushing-the-limits-of.md", "equation": "Home-field advantage:** modeled as level shift Φ^{hfa}_·(v) = Φ_·(v+ησ), η ≥ 0 (eq. 67); experiments use η=0.3. **Scale invariance:** K = K̃σ normalization makes predictions σ-independent (experiments: σ=600, K̃=0.125).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0603-understanding-and-pushing-the-limits-of.md", "equation": "Only low-draw seasons benefit from matched κ:** 2013–14 (p̄_D=0.17, κ̄≈0.42) and 2018–19 (κ̄≈0.42): κ̄-Elo beats κ=1 by a visible margin (2013–14: κ=0.7 → LS̄=0.93 (0.17,1.86); κ=1 → 0.96 (0.21,1.82); Elo+κ̌ → 0.95; Bet365 → 0.91 (0.14,1.98)).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0603-understanding-and-pushing-the-limits-of.md", "equation": "NFL translation note: p̄_tie ≈ 0.005 → eq. 64 gives κ̄ ≈ 0.01 ≈ 0 — the entire draw apparatus collapses to binary Elo. The portable results are the SG-ML framing, the E[s_i]=Φ(Δ) vs Pr(win) distinction, and the K̃σ/η parameterization.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0603-understanding-and-pushing-the-limits-of.md", "equation": "Couple the canonical Elo with a time-varying K̃_t that scales with information content: K̃_t = K̃_0 × (1 + α· | ), where surprise =", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0604-finding-your-feet-a-gaussian-process.md", "equation": "Can a Bayesian model quantify how a cricketer's batting ability varies both within an innings (\"getting your eye in\") and between innings over an entire career (form, age, experience), in intuitive batting-average units — beating both the career batting average and the opaque ICC ratings? The paper fits a Gaussian process over career-innings time to a hazard-based scoring model, yielding per-innings ability estimates ν(t) with credible intervals, career-low/high quantification, next-innings predictions, and principled player comparisons (e.g., P(Smith outscores Williamson) = 56.5%).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0604-finding-your-feet-a-gaussian-process.md", "equation": "Likelihood:** hazard H(x) = P(X=x|X≥x) (eq. 1); not-out scores treated as right-censored, likelihood P(X≥x) (eqs. 2–3).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0604-finding-your-feet-a-gaussian-process.md", "equation": "Effective average:** H(x) = 1/(μ(x)+1) (eq. 4); μ(x) = μ₂ + (μ₁−μ₂)exp(−x/L) (eq. 5): μ₁ = initial ability, μ₂ = \"eye-in\" equilibrium ability, L = e-folding transition time.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0604-finding-your-feet-a-gaussian-process.md", "equation": "Between-innings:** μ(x,t) = μ_{2t} + (μ₁−μ_{2t})exp(−x/L) (eq. 6), with per-innings skill-ceiling μ_{2t}; μ₁, L held constant across career (computational parsimony; getting-eye-in is style-driven).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0604-finding-your-feet-a-gaussian-process.md", "equation": "GP prior:** log{μ_{2t}} ~ GP(λ, K), K(tⱼ,t_k) = σ²exp(− | ^α/ℓ^α), α ∈ [1,2] (eq. 7) — powered exponential: α→2 = squared-exponential (too smooth, rejected), α→1 = Ornstein–Uhlenbeck/AR(1) (Matérn). ν(t) = E[score] in innings t, computed analytically.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0604-finding-your-feet-a-gaussian-process.md", "equation": "Context effects:** μ(x,t) = [·] × ψ^{v_t} × φ^{i_t} (eq. 10); v_t ∈ {1,0,−1} home/neutral/away, i_t ∈ {1,−1} first/second innings; ψ>1 = home advantage, φ>1 = first-innings advantage.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0604-finding-your-feet-a-gaussian-process.md", "equation": "Williamson deep-dive (Table 3):** career avg 50.99; C=0.30, D=0.12, λ=56.6, σ=0.27, ℓ=36.7, α=1.50; ψ=1.11 (95% CI 0.93–1.32) → ψ²=1.25 (0.87–1.75) home-vs-away; φ=1.03 → φ²=1.07 (0.74–1.48) first-vs-second innings. Career low ν=34.2, high 73.6, next-innings prediction 47.1 (95% CI 25.3–72.0) (Table 4).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0605-bayesian-isotonic-logistic-regression-via-constrained.md", "equation": "Likelihood:** Y_{ij}|p_{ij}(x) ~ Bernoulli(p_{ij}(x)) (eq. 1); logit p_{ij}(x) = f_i(x) + (α_i − α_j) (eq. 2) — serve-advantage curve + Bradley–Terry rally-ability difference.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0605-bayesian-isotonic-logistic-regression-via-constrained.md", "equation": "Rally ability:** α_i|α₀,σ_α ~ N(α₀,σ²_α) with Σ_i α_i = 0 identifiability (eq. 10); court extension α_{i,c}, c ∈ {clay, grass, hard}, ΣΣα=0 (eqs. 11–12) — surface-specific ability vectors.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0605-bayesian-isotonic-logistic-regression-via-constrained.md", "equation": "Inputs: rally length x, server/receiver IDs, server-win indicator, court surface. Features: B-spline basis evaluations b_m(x), player ability parameters, court indicators. Target: p_{ij}(x) = P(server i beats receiver j at rally length x); secondary targets: total serve advantage f_i(0)−f_i(15), rally abilities α_{i,c}.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0605-bayesian-isotonic-logistic-regression-via-constrained.md", "equation": "Serve advantage magnitude:** P(server wins | x=1) = 0.83 men (95% CI 0.75–0.94), 0.69 women (0.55–0.83); at x=15 (advantage gone): men (0.51,0.64), women (0.46,0.55) — pure rally-ability contests.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0605-bayesian-isotonic-logistic-regression-via-constrained.md", "equation": "Monotone calibration module:** replace binned recalibration with BILR: logit P(win) = Σ β_m b_m(model_prob) with β₁ ≤ β₂ ≤ … ≤ β_M (fully monotone), B-spline order 4, ~9 bases on [0,1], recursive ε-increment prior (mirror of eq. 8 with +ε). Fit in Stan on 2020–2025 game predictions vs. outcomes (spread/ML engine outputs). Output: smooth monotone calibration map + 95% bands; apply to all engine probabilities before publishing.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9128}
